      <section class="preparation-module" aria-labelledby="lawn-reliability">
        <h3 id="lawn-reliability">What if a reading never arrives?</h3>
        <p>
          A reassuring number is only useful if it can be trusted. The app checks freshness and time quality, preserves
          gaps in the history, and withholds watering suggestions when readings are unreliable. A dry trend must remain
          valid for an uninterrupted 30-minute window before the current logic suggests watering.
        </p>
        <div class="engineering-note">
          <p class="small-label">DEVELOPMENT EXAMPLE / A LOST ACKNOWLEDGEMENT</p>
          <h4>Send again. Keep one reading.</h4>
          <p>
            A measurement can reach the database even when its acknowledgement never reaches the device. The local queue
            model and ingestion code are tested together: resend that measurement, keep a single database record, then
            remove only the readings that have been acknowledged.
          </p>
          <p class="note">
            The production ESP32 firmware has native tests, simulated-probe checks and a CI build. On the bench, its
            first uploads were acknowledged and the queue emptied. Flash durability across a power loss remains
            unverified.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p>
          The cloud workspace uses Supabase authentication and owner-scoped database access. A separate public
          projection exposes only the selected garden data; exact coordinates, private diary entries, alerts and
          calibration notes stay outside it. The owner can disable publication. Live shows a waiting message until
          readings arrive.
        </p>
        <p>
          I define the requirements and expected behaviour, carry out bench checks and decide which results are
          supported by the evidence.
        </p>
        <p class="stack">Supabase / PostgreSQL · Access rules · Idempotent ingestion · Local automated checks</p>
        <p class="note">
          The app and cloud services are online, and the production firmware sends readings from the lawn. Calibration,
          continuous field monitoring and flash durability across a power loss remain unverified. Watering thresholds
          remain preliminary; automatic irrigation is not active.
        </p>
      </section>

